{"book":11,"chapter":9,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 9","slides":[{"title":"Modules and Exceptions","sub":"Chapter 9 · Splitting code, honest failures","short":"Intro","main":"Modules split code into parts; exceptions report failures honestly.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One file","Modules","Exceptions"],"captions":["While a program fits in one file it's simple, but a real app has hundreds of files","Modules split code into parts with their own scope and explicit \"takes\" and \"gives\"","Exceptions report failures honestly, so one error doesn't bring down the whole app"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":160.0,"h":60.0,"text":"app.js\n2000 lines","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":66.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":32.0,"text":"api.js","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":196.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":32.0,"text":"ui.js","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":66.0,"y":106.0,"w":110.0,"h":32.0,"text":"utils.js","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":196.0,"y":106.0,"w":110.0,"h":32.0,"text":"store.js","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":32.0,"text":"app.js","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["try {","  save(order);","} catch (e) {","  report(e);","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":270.0}]],"cues":[9.9,28.5]}]},{"title":"ES modules","sub":"export and import","short":"ESM","main":"A module runs once and has its own scope.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["export","import","default"],"captions":["A module has its own scope; to hand something out, write export before a declaration","To take something, write import with braces and names; a module runs once, its result is cached","A module has one default export; import it without braces under any name"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["// math.js","export const PI = 3.14;","export function add(a, b) {","  return a + b;","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["// app.js","import { add, PI } from './math.js';","add(1, 2);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["// logger.js","export default function log(x) {}","","// app.js","import log from './logger.js';"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.0,27.2]}]},{"title":"Live bindings","sub":"import() on demand","short":"Bindings","main":"An import is a live binding, not a copy; import() loads code on demand.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Live binding","Read-only","import()"],"captions":["An import doesn't copy the value: if the module changes the variable, every importer sees the new value","You can't reassign an imported name; imports are hoisted, so a conditional import is impossible","Dynamic import() returns a promise with the module: code loads on demand, e.g. on a click"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["// counter.js","export let n = 0;","export function inc() { n++; }","// app.js","import { n, inc } from './counter.js';","inc(); n   // 1"],"hl":[5],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["import { n } from './counter.js';","n = 5;   // TypeError","","if (ok) import x from 'x';   // SyntaxError"],"bad":[1,3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["button.onclick = async () => {","  const m = await import('./chart.js');","  m.draw(data);","};"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[15.9,34.7]}]},{"title":"CommonJS","sub":"require and module.exports","short":"CommonJS","main":"require is synchronous and returns a copy of the reference.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Wrapper function","require is synchronous","Copy, not binding"],"captions":["A CommonJS file is a function that receives require, module and exports","require reads the file, runs it and returns exports; call it anywhere, even inside an if","Bindings aren't live: you get a copy of the object reference at the moment of the call"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":300.0,"h":90.0,"text":"","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":42.0,"text":"(function (exports, require, module) {","size":9.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"text":"… file code …","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"e","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"})","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const fs = require('fs');","if (debug) {","  const log = require('./log');","}","module.exports = { run };"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["// c.js:  let n = 0; exports.n = n; …","const { n } = require('./c');","// n is a copy of the value at call time","// changes in c.js are not visible"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[12.9,27.9]}]},{"title":"Cycles and barrels","sub":"Circular dependencies","short":"Cycles","main":"Move shared code to a third module; explicit imports beat barrels.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Cycle","Extract shared","Barrels"],"captions":["\"a\" imports \"b\" and \"b\" imports \"a\": CommonJS gives the second a half-built export, ESM a ReferenceError","Avoid cycles: move shared code to a third module, and both sides depend only on it","An index.js re-exporting a whole folder is handy but drags in hundreds of files: explicit imports are better"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":32.0,"text":"a.js","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":32.0,"text":"b.js","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t"